{"statuses": {"73556352": "waiting", "edefa885": "running", "68f6f6c5": "completed", "68a4f486": "completed", "b692f8e1": "crashed", "6497a261": "completed", "1ebfad5b": "running"}, "parent_of": {"73556352": null, "edefa885": "73556352", "68f6f6c5": "73556352", "68a4f486": "73556352", "b692f8e1": "73556352", "6497a261": "73556352", "1ebfad5b": "73556352"}, "names": {"73556352": "Root Agent", "edefa885": "Static-Security-Triage-Agent", "68f6f6c5": "Map-Sites-Exploit-Agent", "68a4f486": "CSV-Injection-Agent", "b692f8e1": "XSS-Render-Posture-Agent", "6497a261": "Authorization-Audit-Agent", "1ebfad5b": "Auth-CSRF-BusinessLogic-Agent"}, "metadata": {"73556352": {"task": "\n\nLocal Codebases: - C:\\Users\\Mayco\\Documents\\Cluster-web-Builder\\.tmp\\strix-target-20260810-130438 (available at: /workspace/strix-target-20260810-130438; this is the user's real directory, mounted live and writable — .git/.agents/.codex are read-only)\n\nSpecial instructions: Perform a defensive white-box security assessment of this local source-code copy. Focus on OWASP Top 10, authentication, authorization/IDOR, injection, SSRF, XSS, CSRF, file upload, secret exposure, and business-logic flaws. Validate findings where safe. Do not modify target source files. Do not contact or test any public production domain; keep dynamic activity inside the sandbox. IMPORTANT TERMINAL RULE: exec_command may return Process running with session ID and no output even for short commands. Whenever it does, immediately call write_stdin with that session_id and empty chars until the command completes; read that output before issuing or repeating another command.", "skills": []}, "edefa885": {"task": "Run comprehensive static analysis: semgrep for vulnerability patterns, gitleaks/trufflehog for secrets, trivy fs for dependency CVEs, and ast-grep for query injection sinks. Output JSON reports to /workspace/.static-analysis/. Identify all hardcoded secrets, vulnerable dependencies, SQL injection sinks, XSS sinks, and IDOR patterns. Report dependency CVEs via create_dependency_report.", "skills": ["source_aware_sast"]}, "68f6f6c5": {"task": "Validate information disclosure in GET /api/map-sites. The route returns businessName + location for ALL sites with non-null location, no auth. Confirm whether DRAFT sites' business names/locations are exposed. If so, file a vulnerability report for unauthorized data exposure of private business metadata.", "skills": ["information_disclosure", "idor"]}, "68a4f486": {"task": "Validate CSV formula injection in GET /api/sites/[siteId]/leads/export. The csvCell function only wraps values in quotes but doesn't neutralize cells starting with = + - @. Validate that a malicious lead submission (via POST /api/public/sites/[slug]/leads) can inject Excel formulas into the exported CSV. File a vulnerability report.", "skills": ["information_disclosure", "xss"]}, "b692f8e1": {"task": "Review the client-side + server-render XSS posture of this Next.js site builder. Examine how published site content is rendered: app/s/[slug]/page.tsx, app/d/[domain]/page.tsx, components/builder/SitePreviewV2.tsx, lib/site/v2-render.ts, lib/site/export-html.ts, lib/site/export-freeform-html.ts, lib/site/section-composer.ts, lib/site/section.ts, and components/builder/SitePreview.tsx. Determine whether any user-controlled content (business name, section titles, body text, CTA links, media URLs, social links, JSON blueprint fields) reaches dangerouslySetInnerHTML or raw HTML interpolation WITHOUT escaping. The v2-render uses escapeHtml/safeUrl — verify completeness. Report any confirmed stored/reflected XSS via create_vulnerability_report.", "skills": ["xss"]}, "6497a261": {"task": "Audit authorization (IDOR / BFLA) consistency across the API. Review every route under app/api/sites/*, app/api/billing/*, app/api/admin/users, app/api/auth/*, app/api/ai/*, app/api/generate-logo, app/api/map-sites, app/api/public/*. Confirm each enforces site ownership (via assertSiteAccess or the inline `user.role === \"ADMIN\" ? {} : { userId: user.id }` pattern). Look for routes that: (a) accept a siteId/sectionId/revisionId and mutate without ownership check, (b) miss auth on data-access endpoints, (c) let an EDITOR escalate. Report any confirmed IDOR/BFLA with create_vulnerability_report.", "skills": ["idor", "broken_function_level_authorization"]}, "1ebfad5b": {"task": "Audit authentication, session, CSRF, and business-logic issues. Review: lib/auth.ts, lib/password.ts (scrypt KDF — check salt/cost/rounds), session cookie flags, password reset flow, admin escalation paths (register defaults to EDITOR, /api/admin/users requires ADMIN), billing webhook logic (checkout.session.completed sets planStatus ACTIVE from client_reference_id), Stripe webhook signature validation, and open-redirect in checkout 'from' param. Determine whether SameSite=lax cookies adequately prevent CSRF on state-changing POSTs and whether any auth bypass / privilege escalation / business logic flaw is exploitable. Report confirmed issues via create_vulnerability_report.", "skills": ["authentication_jwt", "csrf", "business_logic"]}}, "pending_counts": {"73556352": 1, "edefa885": 0, "68f6f6c5": 0, "68a4f486": 0, "b692f8e1": 0, "6497a261": 0, "1ebfad5b": 0}, "recovery_counts": {"b692f8e1": 15, "1ebfad5b": 4, "edefa885": 3}, "idle_resume_counts": {}, "wait_kinds": {"73556352": "agents"}, "mailboxes": {"73556352": [{"from": "b692f8e1", "type": "crashed", "priority": "high", "content": "[Agent crash] XSS-Render-Posture-Agent (b692f8e1) terminated unexpectedly. Stop waiting on this child unless you want to message it again."}]}, "errors": {}, "budget_stopped": false, "reserve_stopped": false, "budget_paused": false}